    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d830">

                <pb facs="1111" n="1005" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg1005"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) City of Flint/73: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-30T15:00:00+03:00">October 30, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 30—11:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>833. The press today contains no reference of [<hi rendition="#italic">to</hi>]
                    the <hi rendition="#italic">City of Flint</hi> or to the Department’s statement
                    issued in connection therewith. The <pb facs="1112" n="1006" xml:id="pg1006"/>
                    Department’s telegram containing the text of the statement issued on the 28th,
                    which was apparently sent from Washington on the evening of that date, was not
                    delivered to the Embassy until 3:30 on the morning of the 30th, having been held
                    up by the Soviet telegraph authorities.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d830-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d830-f1" n="92" xml:id="d830-f1-content">
                <p>This statement was sent to the Embassy in telegram No. 217, October 29, 1939,
                    3:35 p.m. For the text of the statement, see Department of State, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>,
                    p. 431. For other press releases regarding the <hi rendition="#italic">City of
                        Flint</hi>, issued by the Department of State, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, pp. 429–432, 457–458, and 556.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
